{
    "key": "wedding",
    "templateKey": "repobot-wedding",
    "title": "Weddings",
    "description": "A wedding photographer's studio site: full-bleed crossfade hero, sequenced wedding galleries with a lightbox, flat-priced packages with an FAQ, about with testimonials, an inquiry form, and a code-gated client proofing room \u2014 a multi-page site edited in one content file.",
    "marketingExampleTitle": "Wedding photography studio",
    "category": "photography",
    "homePath": "/",
    "previewPath": "/wedding",
    "homeViewDir": "web/app/src/View/Wedding",
    "base": "content",
    "clientOnly": true,
    "capabilities": ["IOS", "ANDROID"],
    "isDefault": false,
    "forms": {
        "$comment": "Managed-form kinds, formKey -> kind (append-only vocabulary: RSVP | LEAD | MAILING_LIST | PROOFING). The studio's inquiry form is a lead pipeline. The proofing room's selection form is declared PROOFING (owner decision, 2026-08-31): client proofing is a managed capability the platform runs for the studio, and the dashboard renders selections as a typed proofing record (client, frame list in album order, new/handled) instead of the raw Inbox's field dump.",
        "inquiry": "LEAD",
        "proofing-selection": "PROOFING"
    },
    "contentContract": {
        "$comment": "The pack's content slots, as data (packs/README.md 'Content contract'). Declares what a composer (agent or tool) must bind for a generated variant of this pack to present as real: slot paths into the typed content module, their kinds, and minimums. Authored alongside the module and guarded by the pack's content tests \u2014 the module satisfies the contract; the contract never drifts ahead of it.",
        "module": "web/app/src/View/Wedding/content.ts",
        "slots": {
            "photographer.name": { "kind": "text" },
            "photographer.tagline": { "kind": "text" },
            "photographer.location": { "kind": "text" },
            "photographer.email": { "kind": "text" },
            "heroSlides": { "kind": "media[]", "min": 1 },
            "selectedWork": { "kind": "media[]", "min": 4 },
            "albums": {
                "kind": "collection",
                "min": 1,
                "item": {
                    "title": { "kind": "text" },
                    "eyebrow": { "kind": "text" },
                    "description": { "kind": "text" },
                    "images": { "kind": "media[]", "min": 4 }
                }
            },
            "home.headline": { "kind": "text" },
            "home.subheadline": { "kind": "text" },
            "home.intro.title": { "kind": "text" },
            "home.intro.paragraphs": { "kind": "text[]", "min": 1 },
            "packages": {
                "kind": "collection",
                "min": 2,
                "item": {
                    "name": { "kind": "text" },
                    "price": { "kind": "number" },
                    "description": { "kind": "text" },
                    "features": { "kind": "text[]", "min": 2 }
                }
            },
            "faq": {
                "kind": "collection",
                "min": 3,
                "item": {
                    "question": { "kind": "text" },
                    "answer": { "kind": "text" }
                }
            },
            "about.headline": { "kind": "text" },
            "about.portrait": { "kind": "media" },
            "about.paragraphs": { "kind": "text[]", "min": 2 },
            "about.testimonials": {
                "kind": "collection",
                "min": 1,
                "item": {
                    "quote": { "kind": "text" },
                    "name": { "kind": "text" },
                    "detail": { "kind": "text" }
                }
            },
            "inquire.headline": { "kind": "text" },
            "inquire.body": { "kind": "text" }
        }
    },
    "theme": {
        "$comment": "The lanternlight register's overlay: mode dark opens the site in its native midnight appearance (string lights against night sky \u2014 the appearance toggle still swaps to the morning-after light variant), and the preset's ink-on-ground monochrome rides as the project brand so app-side surfaces (the code-gated proofing room's chrome and controls) wear the same register as the marketing pages instead of the kernel default blue. Brand values match the lanternlight preset's own light/dark accents \u2014 the marketing pages resolve brand over preset accent, so keeping them identical means the overlay re-brands the app without shifting the pages.",
        "mode": "dark",
        "brand": { "primary": "#1a1a1a", "primaryDark": "#f4f4f4" }
    },
    "landing": {
        "$comment": "Doc-aware pack pages: routes maps each pack route to the page id its config merges under (web/app/src/View/Wedding/WeddingPage.tsx, useSitePageConfig). pages seeds each page's layout skeleton \u2014 ids match weddingLanding.ts; the platform's structural editor edits these. style must ride the overlay: the compose merge keeps the kernel document's root style otherwise, and applySitePageDocument makes the document preset outrank every page's pinned one. The preset is lanternlight (the nighttime-celebration register: midnight ground, white string-light glow, staid black-and-white palette, marquee masthead, tilted party prints, ticket-stub RSVP) \u2014 the wedding as the night itself; heirloom, the keepsake after the day, stays in the kernel as its remix-adjacent register.",
        "style": { "preset": "lanternlight" },
        "routes": {
            "/": "home",
            "/weddings": "weddings",
            "/packages": "packages",
            "/about": "about",
            "/inquire": "inquire"
        },
        "pages": {
            "home": {
                "sections": [
                    {
                        "id": "hero",
                        "type": "hero",
                        "variant": "masthead-overlay"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "intro",
                        "type": "content-split",
                        "variant": "media-left"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "selected-work",
